# 7️⃣ 🔀 Cross Analysis

The cross-analysis section focuses on relationships between multiple customer attributes.

## Q34. Which occupation has the highest average income among females?

```sql
SELECT 
    Occupation,
    ROUND(AVG(AnnualIncome), 1) AS highest_average_income
FROM adventureworks_customer
WHERE Gender = 'F'
GROUP BY Occupation
ORDER BY highest_average_income DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

---

## Q35. Which occupation has the highest average income among males?

```sql
SELECT 
    Occupation,
    ROUND(AVG(AnnualIncome), 1) AS highest_average_income
FROM adventureworks_customer
WHERE Gender = 'M'
GROUP BY Occupation
ORDER BY highest_average_income DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

---

## Q36. Which age group has the highest average income?

```sql
SELECT 
    CASE
        WHEN Age BETWEEN 40 AND 49 THEN '40-49'
        WHEN Age BETWEEN 50 AND 59 THEN '50-59'
        WHEN Age BETWEEN 60 AND 69 THEN '60-69'
        WHEN Age BETWEEN 70 AND 79 THEN '70-79'
        WHEN Age >= 80 THEN '80+'
        ELSE 'Other'
    END AS AgeGroup,
    ROUND(AVG(AnnualIncome), 1) AS highest_average_income
FROM adventureworks_customer
GROUP BY AgeGroup
ORDER BY highest_average_income DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

---

## Q37. Which education level has the most homeowners?

```sql
SELECT 
    EducationLevel,
    COUNT(*) AS homeowner_count
FROM adventureworks_customer
WHERE HomeOwner = 'Y'
GROUP BY EducationLevel
ORDER BY homeowner_count DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

---

## Q38. Which marital status has the higher average income?

```sql
SELECT 
    MaritalStatus,
    ROUND(AVG(AnnualIncome), 1) AS higher_average_income
FROM adventureworks_customer
GROUP BY MaritalStatus
ORDER BY higher_average_income DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

